  "reference_protocol": "Both public file modes are compared statement-by-statement against SQLite 3.53.4, including return code, complete output, first diagnostic, persisted catalog/rowids/rows and integrity. Fresh final seed differs from development. No expected-answer route, filter or output correction is used.",
  "implementation": [
    "Private materializations derive field collations from the actual first projection and attach ordinary quoted CREATE TABLE text through CoreSourceSQL.retain; its parse equality independently checks the physical schema. Selected row values remain raw and public CTAS definitions remain BINARY.",
    "A fuel-bounded source compiler separates preparation from execution. Preparation validates real source names/functions at LIMIT 0; execution binds actual lexical parents. Scalar query validation returns the real prepared input state/query so IN metadata is read from the correct private schema. Outer scalar-result collation remains separate.",
    "Multiple WITH declarations parse into nested existing CTE nodes with duplicate-name checks and independent comma replay. Reachable body dependencies control which declarations are materialized.",
    "Recursive fields retain first-projection metadata while global UNION duplicate keys use actual full-compound comparison metadata. Recursive UNION terms lower to ALL and enqueue through one collated FIFO seen set. Recursive terms are prepared before evaluating the seed, including an empty seed.",
    "JOIN search keys retain original comparison operands. Swapped index-side constraints and their eligibility checks use the original collation, preserving implicit left/right priority without evaluating operands twice.",
    "Derived CTAS evaluates in a private state and emits ordinary Core CREATE/INSERT commands into the original connection before checked CTAS catalog retention and counter accounting."
  ],
  "primary_source_basis": "Pinned upstream src/select.c sqlite3SubqueryColumnTypes chooses field collation from the leftmost projection; generateWithRecursiveQuery uses multiSelectCollSeq for the Distinct queue and lowers recursive operators to ALL. These facts are retained as executable oracle controls.",
  "proof_scope": "Registered component equations preserve output names when carrying collations, retain all UNION ALL queue rows, suppress an already-seen collated queue row, preserve identity source compilation, and choose original JOIN comparison collation. The existing executeRead_preserves_state and checked catalog-retention contracts remain. The new Lean group exercises actual metadata caches, lexical/lazy scopes, recursive errors, JOIN operand order and CTAS isolation. No full SQLite equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "feature_probe_scope": "The 88-case unittest and fresh survey share named families and one generator. Their 14 failures do not measure global compatibility.",
